      "criterion": "ST-001.3. `SKILL.md` changes in four places and no others: the frontmatter's two-line `metadata:` block (upstream's skill version, 0.4.0) is removed, because CI-001's stdlib reader can't read a nested map, and `NOTICE` records that version; one HTML comment under the frontmatter saying the file is modified from upstream and where; one sentence added to `description` ruling out MoxyWolf published prose (blog posts, articles, papers, email, LinkedIn posts and anything written in Dorian's voice); and a `## MoxyWolf scope` section after the title naming what it's for here (DESIGN.md items and amendments, goal briefs, review contracts and acceptance criteria, SKILL.md files and command descriptions, tool descriptions and error messages) and what it's never for. The section says it overrides upstream's broader triggers: blog posts, articles, papers, email and LinkedIn posts are excluded even when an agent reads them, drafts included. Upstream's own warnings stay as written, including that the skill and its linter check structure only and don't establish ASD dictionary compliance. The description stays within CI-001's 1,024 characters, and the diff against upstream shows those four changes only.",
